Purpose: Land spec-patch-12 (ledger D-05) on road_kit_dev: the road_decisions table and its
  idempotency index, road_decision_api and its tests, and error_api without the -20003 -> 422
  mapping.
Approach: Create the table and index through their ORA-955-tolerant create scripts, compile
  both packages and their test packages, list compile errors, then run error_api_test and
  road_decision_api_test.
Reason: Business rejections become HTTP 200 outcomes with a decision record (GSC definition
  0.1.0 sections 5.4 and 6.7). road-tracker needs this in a tagged road-kit release.
Expected objects:
  ROAD_DECISIONS (table, new), ROAD_DECISIONS_IDEMPOTENCY_UX (index, new)
  ROAD_DECISION_API, ROAD_DECISION_API_TEST (packages, new)
  ERROR_API, ERROR_API_TEST (bodies, replaced)
Risk: Low. Additive apart from error_api; nothing in road-kit raises -20003 except
  error_api_test, checked by grep. Test rows are committed by the autonomous rejection write
  and removed by the suite's own teardown.
Prior history checked: db-history-similar for "decision" and "error_api" -- no decisions table
  has been deployed here; error_api last changed in 20260819_152905 (ORA-8601 mapping). The
  20260829 ORA-12839 failure (ADB parallel DML) is why road_decision_api_test.setup disables
  parallel DML, as the other suites do.
[END INTENT]

